    "name": "Poblano Peppers",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Similar to a green bell pepper with a little more kick. Cooking poblanos mellows them even more, making them slightly sweet. Ripe poblanos are red and tend to be spicier than unripe, green peppers. They're often dried as ancho chiles, and they add a peppery, slightly smoky flavor to dishes. Poblano peppers are mildly spicy, measuring 1,000–1,5000 on the Scoville scale</span></p>",
